48
00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.800
And the reason why it cost money is it's for charity.

49
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.829
So they are raising charity.

50
00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:08.520
So that's really amazing,

51
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.890
they're raising charity for mental health awareness.

52
00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.560
I love this story.

53
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.770
Now this is politics we can get behind.

54
00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.840
Okay, this next story actually comes from Toronto.

55
00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.840
CBC reports that a carpenter named Khalil Sevewright

56
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.860
is building insulated shelters

57
00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.670
for homeless people in the community.

58
00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:30.230 line:15%
And his designs work off body heat,

59
00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:33.650 line:15%
which keeps it around 60 degrees in the winter.

60
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.290 line:15%
And the shelters aren't authorized by the city,

61
00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:37.350 line:15%
but Khalil says

62
00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:41.300 line:15%
that they're a temporary solution for survival.

63
00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.510 line:15%
This is wonderful.

64
00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.470 line:15%
This is the kind of stuff I need to hear.

65
00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:49.150
Absolutely, I mean, it makes me incredibly emotional.

66
00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:53.030
By the way, I am a little worried about my hand turkey.

67
00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:56.730
I don't know if I'm doing this well.

68
00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.450
I'm also trying to make a bow tie,

69
00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.130
